description:
Operator request from downstream project (darth-feedor 2026-05-21). The current memoryPromptMessage() in .xtrm/hooks/beads-gate-messages.mjs prints a 10-line checklist via stderr from the Stop hook every time a claim closes. After one session the checklist (Hard to rediscover / Not obvious / Affects future decision / Still relevant in ~14 days + SKIP examples) is fully internalized; remaining noise crowds the terminal UI.

Patch already applied locally in darth-feedor (commit 9466cb1):

```js
export function memoryPromptMessage(claimId, sessionId) {
  const claim = claimId ? `${claimId} ` : '';
  const ack = `bd kv set "memory-gate-done:${sessionId}"`;
  return `● Memory gate: ${claim}closed. ack: \`${ack} "saved:<key>"\` | \`${ack} "nothing novel - <reason>"\`\n`;
}
```

Both ack forms preserved (saved + nothing-novel). Hook still exits 2 to block-and-prompt; behavior unchanged. Apply upstream so xt update doesn't restore the verbose form on downstream syncs.

Smoke test:
```bash
node -e "import('./.xtrm/hooks/beads-gate-messages.mjs').then(m => console.log(m.memoryPromptMessage('test-id', 'sid-abc')))"
# expected: ● Memory gate: test-id closed. ack: `bd kv set "memory-gate-done:sid-abc" "saved:<key>"` | `bd kv set "memory-gate-done:sid-abc" "nothing novel - <reason>"`
```

