## Context

Companion test issue for xtrm-wdt7.2 (shell wiring layer). Tests the fully-wired CLI end-to-end by spawning the built binary. Layer: **shell**.

## What to build

Add a shell integration test in \`cli/src/tests/hello.test.ts\` (or a separate \`hello-integration.test.ts\`):

\`\`\`typescript
import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';

const BIN = resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', 'dist', 'index.cjs');

describe('xtrm hello (integration)', () => {
  it('prints Hello and exits 0', () => {
    const result = spawnSync('node', [BIN, 'hello'], { encoding: 'utf8' });
    expect(result.stdout.trim()).toBe('Hello');
    expect(result.status).toBe(0);
  });
});
\`\`\`

**Requires:** build must run before test (\`cd cli && npm run build && npx vitest run\`).

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Spawning \`node dist/index.cjs hello\` outputs \`Hello\` with exit code 0
- [ ] Test passes in CI after build step

## Approach notes

- Layer: **shell** — full process spawn, tests the wired command
- Same spawnSync pattern used in \`policy-parity.test.ts\`
- Must run AFTER xtrm-wdt7.2 is complete and built

## Context

Companion test issue for xtrm-wdt7.1 (core layer). Tests the \`createHelloCommand\` factory in isolation, without spawning a process. Layer: **core**.

## What to build

Create \`cli/src/tests/hello.test.ts\` using Vitest (already configured via \`vitest.config.ts\`):

\`\`\`typescript
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import { createHelloCommand } from '../commands/hello.js';

describe('createHelloCommand', () => {
  it('returns a Command named hello', () => {
    const cmd = createHelloCommand();
    expect(cmd.name()).toBe('hello');
  });

  it('action prints Hello to stdout', async () => {
    const spy = vi.spyOn(console, 'log').mockImplementation(() => {});
    const cmd = createHelloCommand();
    // invoke the action directly
    await (cmd as any)._actionHandler([]);
    expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledWith('Hello');
    spy.mockRestore();
  });
});
\`\`\`

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Test file exists at \`cli/src/tests/hello.test.ts\`
- [ ] \`cd cli && npx vitest run\` passes
- [ ] Both test cases green (name check + stdout spy)

## Approach notes

- Framework: Vitest (see \`cli/vitest.config.ts\`)
- Existing test pattern: \`cli/src/tests/policy-parity.test.ts\`
- Layer: **core** — test the factory directly, no process spawning needed
